Relevant columns and their potential usage for the task  
• "date": needed to filter records from 2022‑01‑01 forward and to aggregate by month.  
• "category_name": liquor category whose monthly share of total volume will be compared.  
• "volume_sold_liters": numeric measure of volume to calculate each category’s monthly percentage of total sales volume.  
• "sale_dollars": alternative measure of sales; can be used to cross‑check results.  
• "category": numeric category code (handy when grouping or joining).  

Typical conditions that may be used  
• "date" >= '2022‑01‑01' – restricts data range.  
• "date" < DATE_TRUNC('month', CURRENT_DATE) – keeps only fully completed months.  
• "category_name" IS NOT NULL – removes incomplete rows.  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each returns ≤20 rows) that progress from simple inspection to building the final result.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double quotes and every query is preceded with a short comment.

